<DocsLayout title="Privacy Policy — Kuberfy" description="Kuberfy's privacy policy for the dashboard, mobile app, and self-hosted server.">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p><em>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</em></p>

  <p>
    Kuberfy is self-hosted software. The Kuberfy mobile app and web dashboard connect directly to a Kuberfy server that you install and control on your own infrastructure.
    FasteryDev, LLC ("we", "us"), the maker of Kuberfy, does not operate, have access to, or receive any data from your Kuberfy server.
  </p>

  <h2>Data We Do Not Collect</h2>

  <p>We do not have a backend of our own for the app or dashboard. As a result, we do not collect, store, process, or have access to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account credentials, email, or password</li>
    <li>The projects, applications, deployments, or logs you manage in Kuberfy</li>
    <li>Your server's IP address, domain names, or traffic data</li>
    <li>Any analytics, usage tracking, or advertising identifiers</li>
  </ul>

  <p>The mobile app does not include any analytics, advertising, or crash-reporting SDKs.</p>

  <h2>Data Stored on Your Device</h2>

  <p>The Kuberfy mobile app stores the following locally, on your device only, using the operating system's secure storage:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The URL of the Kuberfy server you connect to</li>
    <li>Your authenticated session token</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This information never leaves your device except to communicate directly with the Kuberfy server you configured. If your device supports Face ID or Touch ID, the app
    may use it to lock local access to the app; biometric data is handled entirely by your device's operating system and is never accessible to us or transmitted anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Handled by Your Kuberfy Server</h2>

  <p>
    Your Kuberfy server (which you install and administer) stores account credentials, project configuration, deployment history, and logs in its own embedded database, on
    infrastructure you control. Because you operate that server, you are the data controller for any information it stores. Refer to your own organization's policies for
    how that data is handled.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-Party Sharing</h2>

  <p>We do not sell, rent, or share any data with third parties, because we do not collect any in the first place.</p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

  <p>Kuberfy is a developer/operations tool and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

  <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page and revise the "Last updated" date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent via <a href="https://github.com/JoelVeloz/kuberfy/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Issues</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
